    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194-a1">

                <pb facs="0394" n="1354" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1354"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 193–Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cañate to Mr.
                            Bacon.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Republic of Paraguay, Office of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Asuncion</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1887-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 14, 1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’affaires</hi>: I comply with a duty in
                    advising you that the Chamber of Deputies have not approved the protocol, in
                    regard to the United States and Paraguayan Navigation Company, signed by your
                    excellency and my honorable predecessor in the charge of the office of foreign
                    relations, dated August 12 last, by reason whereof that arrangement remains
                    ineffectual.</p>
                <p>Deploring that the solution which it gave to that claim has not been approved, it
                    pleases me to assure, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Augustin Canate.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
